      "notes": "Orion vendor GUI assigned type 4 instance 0 to channel 1 during temporary loads. The Darkface 65 2x12 load produced five 0x08/0xf6/type4/instance0 envelopes with segment indices 0..4 and two additional opaque envelopes (0x65/0x53 and 0x3c/0x2a). Eleven cabinet labels and both five-option mic menus are recorded as displayed UI choices, not device readback. A bounded Mic A inverse ended at -1 dB, and a separate Mic B level inverse ended at -5 dB from -6 dB; no further level gestures were sent. A Mic B model selector round trip and bounded ReSpire, HPF, LPF, unlabeled Mic B-row icon, and panel BP click/inverse pairs returned their UI crops and observed inverse report sets to fresh-load captures. The icon has no assigned meaning; the envelopes and BP event bytes remain opaque. Trials were removed, AFX 2 verified empty and the original empty AFX 1 view restored. Load/write contracts, parameter meanings and encodings, independent readback, physical scaling/restoration, audible behavior and license ownership remain unverified.",
